 solution_overview: "**Given:** Uma, Victor, Wendy, Xavier, Yara, Zane and Bianca decide about a tournament. 1. Uma competes if and only if Victor competes. 2. If Victor competes, then Wendy competes. 3. Exactly one of Wendy or Xavier competes. 4. If Xavier competes, then Yara does not. 5. At least one of Yara or Zane competes. 6. Zane competes only if Bianca does not compete. 7. If Bianca competes, then Uma competes. 8. At least four of the seven compete.\n\n**Rule:** In symbols: (1) Uma $\\Leftrightarrow$ Victor; (2) Victor $\\Rightarrow$ Wendy; (3) exactly one of Wendy, Xavier; (4) Xavier $\\Rightarrow \\neg$ Yara; (5) Yara $\\lor$ Zane; (6) Zane $\\Rightarrow \\neg$ Bianca, with **contrapositive** Bianca $\\Rightarrow \\neg$ Zane; (7) Bianca $\\Rightarrow$ Uma, with contrapositive $\\neg$ Uma $\\Rightarrow \\neg$ Bianca; (8) the roster has at least 4 members.\n\n**Work:**\n\nStep 1. Test \"Victor does not compete\". Rule (1) then puts Uma out, and rule (7)'s contrapositive puts Bianca out. Rule (3) also removes one of Wendy and Xavier, so at most three of the remaining people can compete. Check both branches.\n\nStep 2. Branch \"Wendy in, Xavier out\": the possible competitors are Wendy, Yara, Zane, giving at most 3, which fails rule (8)'s floor of 4.\n\nStep 3. Branch \"Xavier in, Wendy out\": rule (4) puts Yara out, then rule (5) puts Zane in, leaving only Xavier and Zane, that is 2, which again fails rule (8).\n\nStep 4. Both branches fail, so Victor competes in every valid roster. Rule (1) then puts Uma in, rule (2) puts Wendy in, and rule (3) therefore puts Xavier out.\n\nStep 5. The forced core is Uma, Victor, Wendy in and Xavier out — three competitors so far, so rule (8) needs at least one more from Yara, Zane, Bianca, which rule (5) already guarantees.\n\nStep 6. Constraints left on Yara, Zane, Bianca: rule (5) needs Yara or Zane, and rule (6) forbids Zane together with Bianca. Rule (7) is satisfied because Uma competes, and rule (4) is vacuous because Xavier is out. The surviving choices are: Yara alone; Yara with Bianca; Zane alone; Yara with Zane.\n\nStep 7. So there are four valid rosters, of size 4 or 5. A roster of six would leave exactly one person out, and that person must be Xavier (Uma, Victor, Wendy are locked in, Xavier is locked out), which would put Yara, Zane and Bianca all in — forbidden by rule (6).\n\n**Results:**\n\n- Victor competes in every roster; assuming otherwise leaves at most three competitors.\n- Uma and Wendy are in every roster, and Xavier is out of every roster (rules 1, 2, 3).\n- Bianca $\\Rightarrow \\neg$ Zane is the contrapositive of rule (6), so it always holds.\n- Four valid rosters exist, from the choices Yara; Yara and Bianca; Zane; Yara and Zane.\n- Roster sizes are four or five; six is impossible because it would need Zane and Bianca together.",
